    "line": 215,
    "summary": "R-squared becomes non-finite for constant actual values.",
    "failure_scenario": "For actual values [5, 5] and forecasts [4, 6], total_variation is zero and this expression returns negative infinity with a RuntimeWarning. The function therefore returns an invalid metric despite validating that its inputs are finite, and write_metrics_report can serialize it as non-standard JSON -Infinity."
  },
  {
    "file": "/Users/doob/dev/energy_forecast_ws/dbc151/project/runs/dbc151/forecast_load.py",
    "line": 224,
    "summary": "Backtest availability is checked without checking available training history.",
    "failure_scenario": "A continuous custom dataset beginning on 2016-07-01 has enough 2018 to 2019 data for the final forecast, but the 2017 target's last hour exists, so this check passes and fit_and_forecast aborts on its six-month training history. The entire CLI run fails instead of skipping the unavailable 2017 backtest."
  },
  {
    "file": "/Users/doob/dev/energy_forecast_ws/dbc151/project/runs/dbc151/forecast_load.py",
    "line": 415,
    "summary": "The metrics report can falsely claim a two-year training window.",
    "failure_scenario": "fit_and_forecast exposes a training_years argument and also accepts any history containing at least 365 days, but the report always writes TRAINING_YEARS. A continuous dataset containing only 2019 passes training and produces a one-year ModelRun while the JSON still reports training_window_years as 2; an explicit training_years override is misreported as well."
  },
  {
    "file": "/Users/doob/dev/energy_forecast_ws/dbc151/project/runs/dbc151/forecast_load.py",
    "line": 252,
    "summary": "Mismatched actual and forecast timestamps are silently outer-aligned.",
    "failure_scenario": "If the forecast index is shifted by one hour, DataFrame construction creates the union of both indexes and fills unmatched values and errors with NaN instead of rejecting the mismatch. The caller can then write an incomplete CSV or plot misleading data even though positional metric calculation may already have reported plausible scores."
  },
  {
    "file": "/Users/doob/dev/energy_forecast_ws/dbc151/project/runs/dbc151/forecast_load.py",
    "line": 117,
    "summary": "The holiday feature omits German state-specific public holidays.",
    "failure_scenario": "country_holidays(\"DE\") without subdivisions contains only federal holidays. Epiphany on 2020-01-06 is a holiday in Baden-Württemberg, Bavaria, and Saxony-Anhalt, but every hour receives is_holiday=0. For nationwide demand this loses a material calendar signal; the generated forecast overestimates several daytime hours that day by roughly 4.5 to 5.4 GW."
  }
]

